         ]
      },
      {
         "step": 2,
         "text": "At \\( x = 0 \\), \\( y - (-1) = -2 \\), which is negative, and a solution never crosses the equilibrium \\( y = -1 \\), so \\( y - (-1) = -2 e^{- 2 x^{2}} \\).",
         "mathjson": -2
      },
      {
         "step": 3,
         "text": "This expression is defined for every real \\( x \\), so no restriction arises, and \\( y = -1 - 2 e^{- 2 x^{2}} \\).",
